# horde-march.vrs: undead-hordes D25. The hm-test event (tools/vrclient/scenarios/fixtures/hm-test.json: a HordeMarch
# of 480 units, 380 troops at level 20, 79 elite at 40, 20 strong at 60 and the Bishop of Death at 50, from the pond's
# Point (-1880, -1640) to "the mark" 600 m east (-1280, -1640), radius 30, marchSpeed 2.0, growth 1-3 up to 20, infest
# hunters 60) rises with Chaos 200 m north of the route. Unseen, it marches (the front's percent climbs). Chaos then
# stands 20 m ahead of the front: the front holds (its percent 60 s later is within 2 of the first), and three
# CHAR_Bandit_Thug natives spawned there (`.devnative`) are killed by the horde, which grows by 1-3. Chaos leaves north;
# the horde arrives at the mark and logs the switch to the infestation. `.nyar event stop` drains to 0 tracked.
# After the run, on a copy of BepInEx/LogOutput.log:
#   pwsh tools/preflight.ps1 -TimingSpan <copy> -MinTracked 432          (90 % of the horde)
#   python tools/vrclient/load-ladder.py report <copy>    (step 480: each frame window against D3's bars; the
#                                                          ladder's window counts do not apply to this short run)
# Needs: `python tools/vrclient/fixture-install.py <server>/BepInEx/config/Nyarlathotep/events.json hm-test`; the dev cfg
# at the ladder's ceiling (MaxTrackedUnits 500, MaxUnitsPerWave 500, MaxSpawnsPerTick 20, MaxDespawnsPerTick 20,
# [Debug] TimingLog true; the pillar switch below re-reads it); NyarDevTools (.devtp .devframes .devnative .devnote) and
# DevChatEcho; pillar spawns on; no other event running; Chaos invulnerable (`ToggleInvulnerable true`, never false).
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .nyar pillar spawns on
expect-reply spawns
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
expect-no-log event hm-test: timeout=3
chat .devtp -1580 -1440
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 3
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .devframes on
expect-reply devframes: on
chat .devnote step=480 phase=start
expect-reply devnote: step=480 phase=start
mark
chat .nyar event start hm-test
expect-log event hm-test started by timeout=20
expect-log horde hm-test: 480 units, 1 bosses, from .* to the mark timeout=30
poll-reply RISE tracked units: 480 \(spawning 0, :: .nyar status every=5 timeout=300
chat .devnote step=480 phase=quiet s=${RISE} tracked=480
expect-reply devnote: step=480 phase=quiet
# unseen, the front climbs
expect-log apocalypse hm-test horde 1 front (?P<P1>[0-9]+) % units timeout=60
expect-log apocalypse hm-test horde 1 front (?P<P2>[0-9]+) % units timeout=60
expect-calc ${P2} > ${P1}
# Chaos meets it: 20 m ahead of the front
calc FX = -1880 + 6 * ${P2} + 20
chat .devtp ${FX} -1640
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 3
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .devnote step=480 phase=fight
expect-reply devnote: step=480 phase=fight
expect-log apocalypse hm-test horde 1 front (?P<H1>[0-9]+) % units timeout=60
mark
chat .devnative -301730941 3 300
expect-log \[DEV NATIVE\] n=3
expect-log apocalypse hm-test spread: \+(?P<GROW>[0-9]+) \( timeout=120
expect-calc ${GROW} >= 1 and ${GROW} <= 3
expect-log apocalypse hm-test horde 1 front (?P<H2>[0-9]+) % units timeout=60
expect-calc ${H2} <= ${H1} + 2
shot full hm-held
# Chaos leaves north: the horde marches on and infests at the mark
chat .devtp -1580 -1440
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 3
console ToggleInvulnerable true
expect-log horde hm-test: arrived at the mark after [0-9]+ s, (?P<ARRIVED>[0-9]+) units; infesting timeout=600
chat .devnote step=480 phase=drain
expect-reply devnote: step=480 phase=drain
chat .nyar event stop hm-test
expect-log event hm-test stopped timeout=20
poll-reply DRAIN tracked units: 0 \(spawning 0, despawning 0\) :: .nyar status every=3 timeout=600
chat .devnote step=480 phase=end s=${DRAIN} purged=${ARRIVED}
expect-reply devnote: step=480 phase=end
chat .devframes off
